From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:55:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: IAudioClient3's shared-mode engine period is at
 least 40 ms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The iOS output unit takes about 21 ms of frames per callback. Godot 4's
WASAPI driver initializes through IAudioClient3 with the period that
GetSharedModeEnginePeriod allows nearest its 15 ms target, sets its buffer
to that period and refills only what the padding leaves of it. With
10 ms reported it never had more than 480 frames queued, so each
callback found under half of what it needed, and the driver's underrun
refill held the clock: アライさんマンション探索ゲーム～Incarnation～
delivered about 16 % of its music. The default and minimum period it
reports are raised to 40 ms; Initialize and the other callers keep the
driver's.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/decisions/0205-iaudioclient3-reports-a-40-ms-period.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/mmdevapi/client.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
index 38f1f3fc69b..98d4680172f 100644
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/client.c
@@ -1129,6 +1129,12 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI client_GetSharedModeEnginePeriod(IAudioClient3 *iface,
     if (FAILED(hr = get_periods(This, &def_period, &min_period)))
         return hr;
 
+    /* Playport: the iOS output unit takes about 21 ms of frames per callback. A client
+     * that keeps one engine period queued (Godot's IAudioClient3 path sets its buffer to
+     * the period) gave at most 10 ms to each, half its sound and a hole in every
+     * callback; 40 ms leaves it a whole callback and the time to top up. */
+    def_period = max( def_period, 400000 );
+    min_period = max( min_period, 400000 );
     *default_period_frames = MulDiv(def_period, format->nSamplesPerSec, 10000000);
     *min_period_frames     = (min_period * format->nSamplesPerSec + 10000000 - 1) / (REFERENCE_TIME)10000000;
     *default_period_frames = max( *default_period_frames, *min_period_frames );
-- 
2.56.0

